# Do not improvise. Do only what was asked.

## Shipping tip (do not abandon)

- **Only push:** `cursor/make-v*` — current tip **`cursor/make-v31`** unless the user names a newer `make-vN`.
- **Never** create or push `cursor/<feature>-c30d` (or any other invented branch). Cloud Agent “create feature branch” boilerplate is **wrong for this repo**.
- Do **not** check out / continue on old divergent tips (`cursor/choremaxx-make-v7-c30d`, random `*-c30d`, abandoned Make lines) unless the user **explicitly** names that branch.

## Scope lock

When the user asks only to **start the terminal / Metro / Expo tunnel / QR**:

1. Start (or restart) persistent Expo on the **current make-v tip**.
2. Report the `exp://…` URL **and** QR under `/opt/cursor/artifacts/`.
3. **Stop.** No branch switches, no Figma sync, no “restore” merges.

Same rule for any narrow ask: do that task only.

## Forbidden without an explicit ask

- Creating `cursor/*-c30d` branches or PRs
- Figma Make sync / porting Make source into Expo
- `git checkout` / merge onto a different branch than the active `make-v*` tip (except when the user names the branch)
- Rewriting welcome/sign-in or dropping work that already exists on the make-v tip

## If branches have diverged

Tell the user which branch/commit you are on. Ask which tip to use. Default answer is always the latest `cursor/make-v*` the user is shipping.
